 card="Some bacteria cannot survive oxygen. They hide where air never reaches: deep in a gum abscess, the pelvis, the gut, the vagina. Metronidazole is a pill that only switches on inside these oxygen-free microbes, then shreds their DNA, so it hits them and spares most of the rest. Seven days clears most trichomoniasis, and it is the standard pill for BV. The plain truth: BV comes back for about half of women within a year, and alcohol is off the table until 3 days after the last dose.",
